# Noindex by HOSTNAME, never by path.
#
# One build is served on every address — staging and production are the same
# Worker and the same files — so the only honest place to decide "is this
# staging?" is the hostname the request arrived on. Each rule below names a
# non-production host outright. There is deliberately no `/*` rule: a path-only
# rule matches every host, and on this Worker that includes the live site.
#
# Production (www. and the apex) is never named here and never matched, so
# attaching or detaching a Custom Domain cannot change what either address
# says to a crawler. tests/build/indexability.test.ts and
# scripts/launch-check.mjs both refuse a noindex rule that is not scoped to one
# of these hosts.
#
# robots.txt stays allow-all on every host. `Disallow: /` would stop the crawl,
# so this header would never be read.

https://stage.evergreencleaningservice.ca/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# workers.dev and its version-preview URLs (`<version>-<worker>.<account>`).
# Cloudflare's own documented pattern; a placeholder never spans a dot, so this
# cannot match a *.evergreencleaningservice.ca host.
https://:version.:subdomain.workers.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
